NetHunter Kali chroot: make dbus start on Android.

Symptom:  service dbus start  ->  "dbus is not running ... failed!"
Cause:    dbus-daemon runs as root and then tries to drop capabilities.
          Android's SELinux policy refuses capset (even with CapEff=ffffffffffffffff),
          so it dies with:
              Failed to drop capabilities: Operation not permitted
Fix:      start dbus-daemon directly as the messagebus user, so there is nothing
          to drop. start-stop-daemon gets --chuid $DAEMONUSER.

Applied in /data/local/nhsystem/kali-arm64/etc/init.d/dbus
(original kept as /etc/init.d/dbus.orig inside the chroot)

--- a/etc/init.d/dbus
+++ b/etc/init.d/dbus
@@ start_it_up()
   log_daemon_msg "Starting $DESC" "$NAME"
   start-stop-daemon --start --quiet --pidfile $PIDFILE \
-    --exec $DAEMON -- --system $PARAMS
+    --chuid $DAEMONUSER --exec $DAEMON -- --system $PARAMS
   log_end_msg $?

Verification:
  service dbus start   -> "Starting system message bus: dbus."
  service dbus status  -> "dbus is running."
  /run/dbus/pid and /run/dbus/system_bus_socket owned by messagebus:messagebus
